{"name":"Salami","hex":"#820000","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Salami","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Salami"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salami","blocks":[{"text":"Salami is a salume consisting of fermented and air-dried meat, typically pork. Historically, salami was popular among Southern, Eastern, and Central European peasants because it could be stored at room temperature for a period of time once cut, supplementing a potentially meager or inconsistent supply of fresh meat. Countries and regions across Europe make their own traditional varieties of salami."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Salame_di_Sauris.jpg/330px-Salame_di_Sauris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salami","wikidata":"Q188655"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Here%27s_your_change%21.jpg/500px-Here%27s_your_change%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Here%27s_your_change%21.jpg/1280px-Here%27s_your_change%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Here%27s_your_change%21.jpg/500px-Here%27s_your_change%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A salami shop in Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHere's_your_change!.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Herz_szal%C3%A1mi_plak%C3%A1t.jpg/250px-Herz_szal%C3%A1mi_plak%C3%A1t.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cf/Herz_szal%C3%A1mi_plak%C3%A1t.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb